# =====================================================================
# Release V000 -- Metadata seed baseline (environment-invariant)
# =====================================================================
# Seeds the ETL control + business/config reference tables that the
# Fabric DATA pipelines do NOT populate. The pipelines move source data
# (Bronze->Silver->Gold); these control/config tables must be seeded
# separately, or orchestration + lookups have nothing to run against.
#
# Re-runnable: every file below is idempotent (DELETE+INSERT full
# refresh, or MERGE). So this manifest always brings the target to the
# CURRENT committed seed content -- editing an existing seed file is
# automatically covered on the next run. Adding a brand-NEW seed table
# is the only manual step: add one DEPLOY line below.
#
# Deliberately an EXPLICIT list, not a *.Data.sql glob: three seed files
# are ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC and must NOT be deployed from these dev values
# (they are managed per-environment, e.g. via the app / Fabric config):
#     Audit.Tenants.Data.sql            (dev tenants + dev API secrets)
#     Security.Clients.Data.sql         (dev client orgs)
#     Security.Application_Users.Data.sql (dev user-to-client mappings)
# A glob would leak those into prod; an explicit list cannot.
#
# PREREQUISITE: the target warehouse already has the schema (tables).
# This manifest seeds data only -- it does not create objects.
#
# Run (set FABRIC_SERVER for the target environment first):
#   $env:FABRIC_SERVER = '<endpoint>'   # omit for the dev default
#   .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V000__metadata_seed_baseline.manifest
# No TEST gate here: the regression tests assert against deterministic
# T11 data and would not reconcile against another environment.
# =====================================================================

# 1. ETL orchestration control (Category/Type before Config; Config before Dependency)
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Category.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Type.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Config.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Dependency.Data.sql

# 2. Business / KPI + standard-mapping reference config
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Metric_Period_Types.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Metric_Definitions.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Acquisition_Source_Standard.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Cancellation_Reason_Standard.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Payment_Plan_Standard.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Config.Treatment_Category_Standard.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Silver.Appointment_Reason_Map.Data.sql

# 3. Regression-test framework definitions (only used if Run_Tests targets
#    this warehouse; harmless config otherwise)
DEPLOY  Fabric\Test.Comparison_Definition.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Test.Metric_Definition.Data.sql
